  "notes": "Full-process capture from the EasyMesh Extender Hardware Measurement Report (Appendix A), 40 processes with nonzero RSS out of 140 total captured via /proc at 22:42:54 UTC on 2 Sep 2026 (zero-RSS kernel threads excluded from this list). This supersedes the earlier 4-process, 87.43 MiB Wi-Fi/EasyMesh-only snapshot. totalRssMB (189.65) is the gross sum of individual process RSS values and is higher than the system-level 176 MiB 'used' figure from free/meminfo at capture time, because RSS double-counts shared library and file-backed pages across processes -- it is not a measure of unique physical memory. One process name (onewifi_em_agent) was corrected from a truncated column value using the exact spelling given elsewhere in the same report; other long process names may still appear truncated exactly as captured in the source table (e.g. fixed-width column cutoff), since the correct full spelling isn't independently confirmable elsewhere in the document."
